- How would you optimize for a specific CPU architecture (e.g., using intrinsics)?
- How would you extend this to 256-bit values?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests compact, branch-free parity calculation using classic bit-twiddling techniques.

## Key Concepts
- Parity calculation through XOR folding
- Bitwise shifts and XOR operations
- Elimination of loops and conditional branches

## Code Example
```javascript
function parity32(n) {
  n ^= n >>> 16;
  n ^= n >>> 8;
  n ^= n >>> 4;
  n ^= n >>> 2;
  n ^= n >>> 1;
  return n & 1;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend this implementation to 64-bit parity calculation?
- Design an approach for computing streaming parity over a byte array?
